LeetCode 1831 — Maximum Transaction Each Day (Medium):

Table: Transactions
+----------------+----------+
| Column Name    | Type     |
+----------------+----------+
| transaction_id | int      |
| day            | datetime |
| amount         | int      |
+----------------+----------+
transaction_id is the primary key for this table. Each row contains information about one transaction. LeetCode

Task
Write an SQL query to report the IDs of the transactions with the maximum amount on their respective day. If in one day there are multiple such transactions, return all of them. Return the result table in ascending order by transaction_id. LeetCode
The query result format is in the following example.

Example
Input — Transactions table:
+----------------+--------------------+--------+
| transaction_id | day                | amount |
+----------------+--------------------+--------+
| 8              | 2021-4-3 15:57:28  | 57     |
| 9              | 2021-4-28 08:47:25 | 21     |
| 1              | 2021-4-29 13:28:30 | 58     |
| 5              | 2021-4-28 16:39:59 | 40     |
| 6              | 2021-4-29 23:39:28 | 58     |
+----------------+--------------------+--------+
Output:
+----------------+
| transaction_id |
+----------------+
| 1              |
| 5              |
| 6              |
| 8              |
+----------------+

Solution 1
-------------
select transaction_id
from Transactions
where (day, amount) in (select date(day), max(amount)
                      from Transactions
                      group by 1)
order by 1

Solution 2
------------
-- using window function

with CTE as
    (select transaction_id, dense_rank() over(partition by date(day) order by amount desc) as rnk
    from Transactions)

select transaction_id
from CTE
where rnk = 1
order by 1
